BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//eu-ai-act-tracker//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
X-WR-CALNAME:EU AI Act milestones
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:entry-into-force@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20240801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20240802
SUMMARY:The AI Act enters into force
DESCRIPTION:Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 enters into force. Nothing is yet enf
 orceable\; the dates below start the clock on each group of rules. Article
 s: 113. Source: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohibitions-and-literacy@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250203
SUMMARY:Prohibited practices and AI literacy apply
DESCRIPTION:Chapters I and II apply: the Article 5 prohibitions and the Art
 icle 4 AI literacy duty. Article 4 has since been amended\; the consolidat
 ed text frames the provider and deployer duty as taking measures that supp
 ort AI literacy\, with no required level for any individual. Articles: 4\,
  5. Source: https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gpai-and-governance@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250803
SUMMARY:General-purpose AI obligations\, governance and penalties apply
DESCRIPTION:Chapter V (general-purpose AI models)\, Chapter VII (governance
 )\, Chapter XII (penalties)\, notified body rules in Chapter III Section 4
  and Article 78 apply\, except Article 101. Articles: 51\, 52\, 53\, 54\, 
 55\, 56\, 78\, 99. Source: https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11
 3/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:omnibus-in-force@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260727
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260728
SUMMARY:The Digital Omnibus on AI enters into force
DESCRIPTION:Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 amends the AI Act\, signed on 8 July 
 2026. It moves the high-risk dates and adds the new Article 5 prohibitions
 . Articles: 113. Source: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2026/1744/oj
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:general-application@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260803
SUMMARY:General application date: transparency duties and Commission enforc
 ement over general-purpose AI
DESCRIPTION:The general application date in Article 113 arrives. Article 50
  transparency duties apply\, subject to the Article 50(2) transition below
 . Article 101\, the fines for providers of general-purpose AI models\, app
 lies from this date because it was excluded from 2 August 2025. Articles: 
 50\, 101. Source: https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art-50-2-legacy@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261203
SUMMARY:Deadline for Article 50(2) marking on systems already on the market
DESCRIPTION:Providers of generative systems placed on the market before 2 A
 ugust 2026 must comply with the Article 50(2) duty to mark synthetic outpu
 t by this date. Systems placed on the market on or after 2 August 2026 get
  no grace period. Articles: 50\, 111. Source: https://artificialintelligen
 ceact.eu/article/111/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:new-prohibitions@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261203
SUMMARY:New Article 5 prohibitions apply
DESCRIPTION:The new prohibitions added by the Omnibus\, covering AI systems
  that generate non-consensual intimate imagery and child sexual abuse mate
 rial\, apply from this date. Articles: 5. Source: https://artificialintell
 igenceact.eu/article/113/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gpai-legacy@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270803
SUMMARY:General-purpose AI models placed on the market before 2 August 2025
  must comply
DESCRIPTION:Providers of general-purpose AI models that were on the market 
 before 2 August 2025 must take the necessary steps to comply by this date.
  Articles: 53\, 55\, 111. Source: https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/art
 icle/111/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:annex-iii@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271203
SUMMARY:High-risk obligations apply to Annex III use cases
DESCRIPTION:Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to AI systems classified as h
 igh-risk under Article 6(2) and Annex III\, such as employment\, education
 \, credit scoring and essential services. Moved by the Omnibus from 2 Augu
 st 2026. Articles: 6\, 9\, 10\, 11\, 12\, 13\, 14\, 15\, 16\, 17\, 26\, 27
 . Source: https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/113/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:annex-i@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280803
SUMMARY:High-risk obligations apply to AI in Annex I regulated products
DESCRIPTION:Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to AI systems classified as h
 igh-risk under Article 6(1) and Annex I\, such as safety components of reg
 ulated products. Moved by the Omnibus from 2 August 2027. Articles: 6\, 9\
 , 10\, 11\, 12\, 13\, 14\, 15\, 16\, 17. Source: https://artificialintelli
 genceact.eu/article/113/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:public-authority-legacy@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20300802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20300803
SUMMARY:High-risk systems for public authorities already on the market must
  comply
DESCRIPTION:High-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities 
 and placed on the market before the high-risk rules apply must be brought 
 into compliance by this date. Articles: 111. Source: https://artificialint
 elligenceact.eu/article/111/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:large-scale-it-legacy@eu-ai-act-tracker
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20301231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20310101
SUMMARY:AI components of large-scale IT systems must comply
DESCRIPTION:AI systems that are components of the large-scale IT systems li
 sted in Annex X\, placed on the market or put into service before 2 August
  2027\, must be brought into compliance by this date. Articles: 111. Sourc
 e: https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/111/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
